{"id":"8757635b793ed303","group":"92","path":"92/92-cor-nonstandard-exists.md","title":"Nonstandard Models Exist","display":"cor-nonstandard-exists — Nonstandard Models Exist","type":"corollary","metadata":{"type":"corollary","book":"Gödel's Incompleteness Theorems","book_abbrev":"92","label":"92-cor-nonstandard-exists","aliases":["92-cor-nonstandard-exists"],"display":"cor-nonstandard-exists — Nonstandard Models Exist","depends_on":["[[92-thm-compactness]]","[[92-df-standard-model]]","[[92-df-consistent]]","[[92-ax-peano-arithmetic]]","[[92-df-nonstandard-model]]","[[92-df-model]]","[[92-df-assignment]]","[[92-df-interpretation]]","[[92-ex-nonstandard-model]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"corollary"},{"key":"book","html":"Gödel's Incompleteness Theorems"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"92"},{"key":"label","html":"92-cor-nonstandard-exists"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>92-cor-nonstandard-exists</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"cor-nonstandard-exists — Nonstandard Models Exist"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"1a9a64dce00ebd76\" href=\"?note=1a9a64dce00ebd76\" title=\"92-thm-compactness\">92-thm-compactness</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"ccb738ae4bbf923c\" href=\"?note=ccb738ae4bbf923c\" title=\"92-df-standard-model\">92-df-standard-model</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"c7befd96bd551ade\" href=\"?note=c7befd96bd551ade\" title=\"92-df-consistent\">92-df-consistent</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"89c266445c099752\" href=\"?note=89c266445c099752\" title=\"92-ax-peano-arithmetic\">92-ax-peano-arithmetic</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"47757ea7c4cfcbd4\" href=\"?note=47757ea7c4cfcbd4\" title=\"92-df-nonstandard-model\">92-df-nonstandard-model</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"fd60117fc80e6f95\" href=\"?note=fd60117fc80e6f95\" title=\"92-df-model\">92-df-model</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"fdcbc43c728f79fc\" href=\"?note=fdcbc43c728f79fc\" title=\"92-df-assignment\">92-df-assignment</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"2b7f27c890af1dc3\" href=\"?note=2b7f27c890af1dc3\" title=\"92-df-interpretation\">92-df-interpretation</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"fcf794bdb0764404\" href=\"?note=fcf794bdb0764404\" title=\"92-ex-nonstandard-model\">92-ex-nonstandard-model</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak N_G\">\\(\\mathfrak N_G\\)</span> (standard arithmetic model)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PA}\">\\(\\mathrm{PA}\\)</span> (Peano Arithmetic, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"89c266445c099752\" href=\"?note=89c266445c099752\" title=\"92-ax-peano-arithmetic\">92-ax-peano-arithmetic</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Struc}_G,\\mathrm{Assign}_G,\\models_G\">\\(\\mathrm{Struc}_G,\\mathrm{Assign}_G,\\models_G\\)</span> (structures, assignments, and satisfaction)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NonStd}_G\">\\(\\mathrm{NonStd}_G\\)</span> (nonstandard-model predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-11\" data-note=\"47757ea7c4cfcbd4\" href=\"?note=47757ea7c4cfcbd4\" title=\"92-df-nonstandard-model\">92-df-nonstandard-model</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}nonstandard\\text{-}exists}\\vdash\n\\Bigl[\\forall\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{PA}\\,\\forall\\beta\\in\\mathrm{Assign}_G(\\mathbb N)\\;\n(\\mathfrak N_G,\\beta\\models_G\\varphi)\\Bigr]\n\\Longrightarrow\n\\exists\\mathfrak M\\in\\mathrm{Struc}_G\\;\\mathrm{NonStd}_G(\\mathfrak M)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}nonstandard\\text{-}exists}\\vdash\n\\Bigl[\\forall\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{PA}\\,\\forall\\beta\\in\\mathrm{Assign}_G(\\mathbb N)\\;\n(\\mathfrak N_G,\\beta\\models_G\\varphi)\\Bigr]\n\\Longrightarrow\n\\exists\\mathfrak M\\in\\mathrm{Struc}_G\\;\\mathrm{NonStd}_G(\\mathfrak M)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>关键符号：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>存在PA的非标准模型（与<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{N}\">\\(\\mathbb{N}\\)</span>不同构）</li>\n<li>这是把<a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-12\" data-note=\"fcf794bdb0764404\" href=\"?note=fcf794bdb0764404\" title=\"92-ex-nonstandard-model\">92-ex-nonstandard-model</a>的扩张语言构造与紧致性定理合并后的推论；原式把仅是公理集的<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PA}\">\\(\\mathrm{PA}\\)</span>误当成了<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Con}\">\\(\\mathrm{Con}\\)</span>所接收的形式系统</li>\n<li>非标准模型包含&quot;无穷大&quot;元素</li>\n<li>非标准模型的存在本身不推出PA不完备：即使完整理论<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{TA}_G\">\\(\\mathrm{TA}_G\\)</span>也有非标准模型。只有先证明某句<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\gamma\">\\(\\gamma\\)</span>独立，或分别证明<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PA}+\\gamma\">\\(\\mathrm{PA}+\\gamma\\)</span>与<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PA}+\\neg\\gamma\">\\(\\mathrm{PA}+\\neg\\gamma\\)</span>相容，才能据模型的不同真值解释不完备性</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"92-thm-compactness","status":"resolved","id":"1a9a64dce00ebd76","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[92-thm-compactness]]","embed":false},{"target":"92-df-standard-model","status":"resolved","id":"ccb738ae4bbf923c","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[